# @PROJECT_NAME@

STM32 @STM32_CHIP@ project on stm32-sdk @SDK_VERSION@ — the SDK **concurrency
layer end to end**: an EXTI button interrupt defers work into a
`system::SingleThreadExecutor`, a software `system::Timer` debounces it, a
`system::Channel` (ring mode) delivers every press to a reactive component, and
a third component owns its own **deferred-start** FreeRTOS task.

## SDK rules (must follow)

- CMSIS only, HAL/LL forbidden.
- C++20 (gnu++20), C11 (gnu11).
- MMIO access through `driver::reg::set/clear/write/read/get/modify` only.
- No raw pointers to peripherals — references (`GPIO_TypeDef&`).
- Configs without defaults — every field must be explicit.
- `GpioConfig` / `ExtiConfig` are aggregates; wrap in `gpio<{...}>()` / `exti<{...}>()`
  for compile-time validation.
- EXTI ISR priority must be numerically ≥ `configLIBRARY_MAX_SYSCALL_INTERRUPT_PRIORITY`
  (5 on F4) so the handler may call `postFromISR`. This template uses 6.
- Trailing comma after the last designated initializer to keep clang-format multi-line.

